PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real Apple Pay domain-association file from Stripe.

This empty placeholder reserves the path so the route exists pre-launch. The
production file is generated by Stripe when you register the domain for Apple Pay:

  Stripe Dashboard -> Settings -> Payments -> Payment methods -> Apple Pay
  -> "Add a new domain" -> register ameliasaz.com -> download the
  apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association file -> overwrite this file with it.

Until the real file is served at
  https://ameliasaz.com/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
and the domain is registered in Stripe, the Apple Pay button silently will NOT
render on checkout (Google Pay degrades the same way). See
docs/runbooks/production-readiness.md item P-49 (C-V7-14).

Apache note: ensure the front controller / .htaccess does NOT rewrite
/.well-known/* through index.php — it must be served as a static file with
Content-Type text/plain and HTTP 200.
